        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/problem": "What is the value of $\\frac{2}{5}\\int_{8}^{64}\\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)\\sqrt{{log}_{8}\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=\\log_{8}\\left(\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)\\right).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x \\ln{\\left(8 \\right)}}\\,\u27f9\\,\\ln{\\left(8 \\right)}\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $8$ | $64$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}\\int_{8}^{64}\\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)\\sqrt{{log}_{8}\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\int_{8}^{64}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{log}_{8}\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\int_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}8\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{2 \\ln{\\left(8 \\right)}}{5}\\int_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\operatorname{ln}8(2\\sqrt{u})\\right)|_{1}^{2} \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(2\\operatorname{ln}8(\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{1})\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(2(\\sqrt{2}-1)\\operatorname{ln}8\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
